= Setup environment
For this lab, you can use your personal laptop or the laboratory computer. We won't need plenty of different tools, but we will need an IDE and a Python packet manager.

This lab will provide explanation for PyCharm and UV installation. PyCharm is an IDE from JetBrains. It's very powerful, and we recommend you to use it for this course. You're free to use another IDE if you like, but we will only provide support for PyCharm.

UV is a packet manager for Python developed by Astral. It's a modern alternative to pip. It's fast, simple, and easy to use. We will use it for this lab. You can find more information about UV on the official website: https://astral.sh/uv/

We will also need Wireshark during this lab to capture and analyse network traffic. More information are provided on a separate document:
