  #subtask[
    Open the dashboard of the client laptop.
    In the "Modbus TCP / SCADA" tab, enter the *IP address of the server laptop* and port #traffic-port-modbus, then click "Apply Target".
    Select "FC 01 — Read Coils" as Query Target and click "Send Query" (or "Resume Master Poller").
  ]

  #subtask[
    Capture the traffic on the client laptop.
    Select specific display filter to get only the Modbus traffic and show in your report a query and response of a coil read.
  ]
][][
  + No deliverable. The server laptop only needs its dashboard running: the Modbus server listens on `0.0.0.0:1502`.

  + No deliverable. The client dashboard logs the query and shows the 10 coil states read from the server.

  + Capture filter `tcp port 1502`, display filter `modbus` (or `modbus.func_code == 1` for coil reads only).

    Reference capture (loopback, the LAN version only differs in IP/MAC addresses):
    #shell[```text
    Query     client -> server:1502     b25d 0000 0006 01 | 01 0000 000a
    Modbus/TCP (MBAP header)
        Transaction Identifier: 45661 (0xb25d)
        Protocol Identifier: 0               <- always 0 for Modbus
        Length: 6                            <- bytes following: unit id + PDU
        Unit Identifier: 1
    Modbus (PDU)
        Function Code: Read Coils (1)
        Reference Number: 0                  <- first coil address
        Bit Count: 10                        <- number of coils

    Response  server:1502 -> client     b25d 0000 0005 01 | 01 02 4d 01
    Modbus/TCP
        Transaction Identifier: 45661        <- same as the query
        Protocol Identifier: 0
        Length: 5
        Unit Identifier: 1
    Modbus
        Function Code: Read Coils (1)
        [Request Frame: 5]
        Byte Count: 2
        Bit 0..7 : 0x4d = 0100 1101   -> coils 0, 2, 3, 6 ON
        Bit 8..9 : 0x01 = 0000 0001   -> coil 8 ON
    ```]

    The same query and response in Wireshark:
    #image("/res/img/01-homelab/solution/t6-modbus-query.png", width: 100%)
